  "summary": [
   "Dense: almost every note of the subject and of the upper staff has a finger; whole runs are fingered at their first occurrence and left bare later.",
   "The three-note figure C–B–C is fingered 1-3-2 at the start (left hand) and 4-3-4 or (5)4-3-4 in the right hand: the figure is one hand gesture, the thumb kept for the leap after it.",
   "Alternatives in brackets (bars 3, 6, 21, 29, 31) and silent finger changes on held notes (5–4, 4–3) to keep a voice legato while another moves.",
   "Double notes: the lower staff's alto-and-bass thirds and sixths in bars 13–15 are fingered as one hand's double notes (1/4, 1/3, 2/4).",
   "Hand distribution is explicit: notes on the upper staff for the right hand, the lower for the left (his rule from Fugue I, footnote 2); the alto moves between staves (bars 1–2 in the lower staff in treble clef, bars 6–7 in the upper)."
  ],
